COMPLETE TASK LIST — DATASET 4
________________________________________
1. Data Ingestion & Relational Sanity
•	Load each table independently
•	Inspect schema per table
•	Inspect primary keys
•	Inspect foreign keys
•	Validate data types across tables
•	Check index semantics
•	Detect duplicate primary keys
•	Validate surrogate vs natural keys
•	Inspect row counts and growth rates
•	Memory footprint inspection
🚨 Titanic trap avoided: One CSV ≠ one truth.
________________________________________
2. Entity & Granularity Mapping (Critical)
•	Define each entity:
o	user
o	transaction
o	product
o	event
•	Map granularity per table:
o	users → user-level
o	transactions → order-level
o	events → event-level
•	Detect mixed granularity columns
•	Identify bridge tables
•	Identify fan-out risks
•	Document allowed aggregations
•	Identify entity lifecycle boundaries
________________________________________
3. Semantic & Business Validation
•	Validate column meanings
•	Validate business rules:
o	transaction total ≥ sum(items)
o	event timestamps ≤ transaction timestamps
•	Currency & unit consistency
•	Validate boolean logic (refunds, cancellations)
•	Validate state transitions (view → cart → purchase)
•	Detect logically impossible paths
________________________________________
4. Data Quality in Relational Context
•	Missing FK detection
•	Orphan record detection
•	Duplicate natural keys
•	Cardinality inspection per relationship
•	Many-to-many detection
•	Referential integrity enforcement
•	Temporal integrity across tables
•	Late-arriving records detection
________________________________________
5. Pre-Join Analysis (Mandatory)
•	Choose join direction intentionally
•	Validate join key types
•	Check join key uniqueness on both sides
•	Analyze key overlap ratios
•	Simulate joins with indicators
•	Estimate row explosion risk
•	Define aggregation strategy before join
🚨 Temporal dataset trap avoided: time is not the only axis.
________________________________________
6. Row-Wise Combinations
•	Vertical concatenation (partitioned data)
•	Schema alignment
•	Column reconciliation
•	Deduplication strategy
•	Temporal ordering post-concat
________________________________________
7. Column-Wise & Relational Joins
Standard Joins
•	Inner join (diagnostic)
•	Left join (default but dangerous)
•	Right join (diagnostic)
•	Outer join (debugging only)
Cardinality Validation
•	One-to-one
•	One-to-many
•	Many-to-one
•	Many-to-many (explicitly documented)
Join Validation
•	validate= usage (pandas)
•	Join indicator analysis
•	Row count reconciliation
________________________________________
8. Time-Aware Relational Joins
•	As-of joins (events → transactions)
•	Validity-window joins (promotions)
•	Lag-aligned joins
•	Forward-only joins (causal)
•	Overlapping window detection
________________________________________
9. Post-Join Validation & Damage Control
•	Row inflation analysis
•	Null inflation analysis
•	Duplicate creation detection
•	Key coverage analysis
•	Leakage detection
•	Drop helper columns
•	Re-establish entity identity
________________________________________
10. Target Definition in Relational World
•	Choose target entity:
o	user-level churn
o	transaction fraud
o	conversion
•	Label construction logic
•	Temporal alignment of labels
•	Multi-table leakage detection
•	Label stability checks
________________________________________
11. Aggregation Engineering (Where Most Bugs Live)
•	Event → user aggregation
•	Transaction → user aggregation
•	Product → user aggregation
•	Windowed aggregations
•	Causal cutoff enforcement
•	Multiple aggregation resolutions
•	Feature explosion control
•	Aggregation leakage audits
________________________________________
12. Missing Data (Relational Meaning)
•	Missing because “not applicable” vs “unknown”
•	Structural missingness detection
•	Aggregation-induced missingness
•	Missing indicators by source table
•	Impact analysis of join-induced nulls
________________________________________
13. Outlier Detection (Relational)
•	Transaction amount outliers
•	Event burst detection
•	User-level behavioral anomalies
•	Contextual outliers by segment
•	Fraud-like patterns (diagnostic only)
________________________________________
14. EDA Across Entities
•	Distribution per entity
•	Cross-entity correlations
•	Behavioral segmentation
•	Funnel analysis
•	Cohort analysis
•	Survival curves (users)
________________________________________
15. Feature Engineering (Relational)
•	RFM features
•	Session features
•	Conversion rates
•	Behavioral ratios
•	Temporal decay features
•	Hierarchical aggregations
•	Cross-entity interactions
________________________________________
16. Encoding at Scale
•	High-cardinality handling
•	Entity embeddings (conceptual)
•	Target encoding with grouping constraints
•	Frequency encoding
•	Hash encoding diagnostics
•	Drift-aware encodings
________________________________________
17. Feature Selection (Relational Stability)
•	Redundancy pruning across entities
•	Stability across time slices
•	Group-permutation importance
•	Leakage-resistant importance
•	Aggregation depth pruning
________________________________________
18. Splitting & Evaluation (Relational + Temporal)
•	Entity-based splits
•	Time-aware splits
•	Group-aware CV
•	Leakage diagnostics via performance jumps
•	Slice metrics by entity
________________________________________
19. Modeling & Evaluation
•	Baseline models
•	Tree-based relational models
•	Error analysis by entity
•	Bias & variance across segments
•	Interpretability per entity
________________________________________
What This Dataset Teaches That Others Cannot
•	Joins create data, they don’t just combine it
•	Aggregations are irreversible modeling decisions
•	Cardinality errors look like great performance
•	Leakage hides in relationships, not columns

